    "metadata": "{\"summary\":\"Claims that climate change is a \\\"hoax\\\" are widely considered a form of conspiracy theory and are not supported by the overwhelming scientific consensus or factual data on climate change. Numerous studies and reviews have shown that 90%–100% of actively publishing climate scientists agree that human activity is causing significant changes to the Earth's climate.wikipedia+1​\\nOrigins of Climate Change Hoax Claims\\n\\n\\nThe belief that climate change is a hoax stems from conspiracy theories suggesting that scientists and governments are manipulating data or involved in large-scale fraud for personal or political gain.misinforeview.hks.harvard+1​\\n\\n\\nProminent political figures, particularly in the United States, such as President Donald Trump, have referred to climate change as a \\\"hoax,\\\" often framing environmental policies as unfair or harmful to economic interests.economist+2​\\n\\n\\nThese hoax claims are frequently amplified by fossil fuel lobby groups, partisan media, and certain conservative think tanks, aiming to sow doubt about established climate science.wikipedia​\\n\\n\\nScientific Consensus Versus Hoax Claims\\n\\n\\nExtensive and diverse evidence—from rising global average temperatures to increasing frequency of extreme weather events—confirms the reality of climate change and its human causes.sciencedirect+1​\\n\\n\\nAllegations of global scientific fraud or collusion have not been supported by any credible evidence; in fact, climate data and research methods are publicly available and open to scrutiny.wikipedia​\\n\\n\\nSome individuals initially skeptical about climate change have reconsidered their views upon exposure to scientific data and personal experiences with changing weather patterns.bbc​\\n\\n\\nBelief in climate change conspiracies is associated with a range of psychological and social factors, including lower levels of education and analytic thinking, feelings of powerlessness, and distrust of authority.misinforeview.hks.harvard+1​\\n\\n\\nImpact and Public Perception\\n\\n\\nThe persistence of hoax claims undermines efforts to address climate change and exacerbates polarization, preventing effective public dialogue and policy responses.wikipedia​\\n\\n\\nDespite these claims, most scientific and international organizations—including the Royal Society—maintain that climate change is real, dangerous, and primarily driven by human actions.eenews​\\n\\n\\nIn conclusion, the notion that climate change is a \\\"hoax\\\" is a product of misinformation and conspiracy theory; it is not supported by scientific data or expert consensus but continues to be propagated by political and ideological interests.sciencedirect+2​\",\"citations\":[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climate_change_denial\",\"https://misinforeview.hks.harvard.edu/article/understanding-climate-change-conspiracy-beliefs-a-comparative-outlook/\",\"https://www.economist.com/graphic-detail/2025/10/30/how-many-people-are-already-being-killed-by-climate-change\",\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0272494423001779\",\"https://www.bbc.com/news/science-environment-67483064\",\"https://www.eenews.net/articles/con-scam-hoax-trumps-un-speech-on-climate/\"],\"extractionConfidence\":1,\"extractionWarnings\":[]}"
